WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:15.800
When the kids arrived for class, Chef was nowhere in sight.

2
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.481
A man greeted them.

3
00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.721
"Chef is away on a trip.

4
00:00:21.742 --> 00:00:23.222
I'm Nick, and I'm teaching class today."

5
00:00:26.303 --> 00:00:27.223
Bobby cheered.

6
00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:30.424
"Hooray! No grumpy Chef!"

7
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.541
Jason frowned at Bobby.

8
00:00:33.561 --> 00:00:35.563
"That's not nice."

9
00:00:41.068 --> 00:00:42.389
Nick pointed to the screen.

10
00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:46.773
"We're making fruit salsa and baked tortilla chips with cinnamon.

11
00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.976
Who wants to peel and chop the apple?"

12
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.358
Bobby grabbed an apple.

13
00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:55.801
"Let's play catch first!"

14
00:00:56.922 --> 00:01:00.120
He tossed the apple to Izzie.

15
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.440
Izzie laughed and threw it back.

16
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.702
"Uh, can you chop the apple, please?"

17
00:01:06.162 --> 00:01:06.722
Nick said.

18
00:01:06.742 --> 00:01:10.803
"Sure! After we finish our game!"

19
00:01:11.063 --> 00:01:11.803
Bobby said.

20
00:01:12.863 --> 00:01:15.064
Jason was peeling and cutting up a kiwi.

21
00:01:15.084 --> 00:01:17.905
"You wouldn't do that if Chef was here."

22
00:01:19.005 --> 00:01:19.805
Bobby laughed.

23
00:01:22.066 --> 00:01:24.867
"But Chef's not here."

24
00:01:24.907 --> 00:01:29.768
"We should get busy," Izzie said.

25
00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.565
She stopped playing and began peeling the apple.

26
00:01:34.425 --> 00:01:35.906
Nina was eating raspberries.

27
00:01:35.926 --> 00:01:41.468
"Please save some for the salsa," Nick said.

28
00:01:41.488 --> 00:01:43.989
"I will."

29
00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.811
Nina smiled shyly and ate another raspberry.

30
00:01:49.332 --> 00:01:52.253
Bobby picked up two strawberries and put one in each ear.

31
00:01:52.273 --> 00:01:55.254
"These make good earplugs!"

32
00:01:56.975 --> 00:01:57.935
Izzie made a face.

33
00:01:57.955 --> 00:02:01.821
"Yuck! Don't put those in the salsa."

34
00:02:03.462 --> 00:02:04.282
Bobby laughed.

35
00:02:04.982 --> 00:02:08.404
"I'll feed them to the goats."

36
00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:10.444
He left the kitchen.

37
00:02:11.985 --> 00:02:14.266
Jason put the sliced kiwi into a bowl.

38
00:02:16.147 --> 00:02:17.207
Izzie added the apple.

39
00:02:19.328 --> 00:02:20.909
Nina dumped in the raspberries.

40
00:02:20.929 --> 00:02:24.250
"Oops," she said.

41
00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:28.112
"Sorry I ate so many raspberries!"

42
00:02:29.656 --> 00:02:30.316
"Where's Bobby?"

43
00:02:30.757 --> 00:02:31.377
Nick asked.

44
00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:34.579
They all looked out the window.

45
00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.881
Bobby was playing with the goats.

46
00:02:39.762 --> 00:02:41.923
"I'm going outside too," Izzie said.

47
00:02:41.943 --> 00:02:44.344
"Wait for me!"

48
00:02:45.205 --> 00:02:46.145
Nina followed her.

49
00:02:47.446 --> 00:02:50.287
Jason looked at Nick, who seemed unsure what to do.

50
00:02:50.307 --> 00:02:53.069
"Shouldn't you make them come inside?"

51
00:02:54.229 --> 00:02:54.990
Nick shrugged.

52
00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:56.611
"I'll try."

53
00:02:57.631 --> 00:02:58.532
He walked to the door.

54
00:03:02.884 --> 00:03:03.985
"Kids? Could you come back?

55
00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:08.489
Please?" Jason was mad that they were ruining class.

56
00:03:08.509 --> 00:03:11.932
"You guys cut it out—now!"

57
00:03:13.313 --> 00:03:15.094
His friends froze and stared at him.

58
00:03:15.114 --> 00:03:18.957
"I'm finishing the recipe," Jason said.

59
00:03:18.977 --> 00:03:20.819
"You don't have to help.

60
00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.101
Just show some manners!"

61
00:03:29.086 --> 00:03:31.508
A minute later the three of them were back in the kitchen.

62
00:03:32.396 --> 00:03:33.497
They looked embarrassed.

63
00:03:33.517 --> 00:03:36.919
"Sorry, Nick," Bobby said.

64
00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:40.762
"Me too," Izzie and Nina said.

65
00:03:42.403 --> 00:03:45.345
Bobby sliced the strawberries and added them to the fruit bowl.

66
00:03:46.846 --> 00:03:48.948
Nina sprinkled white sugar over the fruit.

67
00:03:50.289 --> 00:03:51.750
Izzie sprinkled brown sugar.

68
00:03:52.951 --> 00:03:56.473
Jason added strawberry preserves and stirred the salsa together.

69
00:03:58.215 --> 00:04:00.076
Nick covered the bowl in plastic wrap.

70
00:04:01.292 --> 00:04:02.993
Then he put it into the refrigerator.

71
00:04:05.054 --> 00:04:06.774
"Now we'll make the cinnamon chips."

72
00:04:08.555 --> 00:04:12.457
Bobby preheated the oven and put parchment paper on two baking sheets.

73
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:17.399
Nick sliced tortillas into triangles to form chips.

74
00:04:19.499 --> 00:04:20.680
He put them on the sheets.

75
00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:25.122
Jason sprayed the chips with cooking spray.

76
00:04:27.043 --> 00:04:30.144
Bobby made the cinnamon sugar and sprinkled it on the chips.

77
00:04:32.232 --> 00:04:33.412
Nina sprayed them again.

78
00:04:35.813 --> 00:04:37.353
Nick put the chips into the oven.

79
00:04:38.954 --> 00:04:40.194
The kids cleaned the kitchen.

80
00:04:42.195 --> 00:04:45.616
When the chips were ready, Nick set out bowls of fruit salsa.

81
00:04:49.677 --> 00:04:51.917
They dipped the cinnamon chips into the salsa.

82
00:04:51.937 --> 00:04:55.238
"Mmm!" Nina said.

83
00:04:55.258 --> 00:05:01.780
"Nick, please don't tell Chef we were misbehaving," Izzie said.

84
00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.041
Nick smiled.

85
00:05:04.061 --> 00:05:07.967
"Okay." Bobby looked at Jason.

86
00:05:07.987 --> 00:05:10.790
"You won't tell either, will you?"

87
00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.435
"I'm not a tattletale," Jason said.

88
00:05:14.455 --> 00:05:17.519
"But you sure made me grumpy today!"
